   \"impact\": \"The FCC firmware addressing the PWM driver at 0x40 would get no response, so the servo outputs would not be driven. The schematic note suggests the 0x41 address may be intentional, so this is less certain.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.25\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The most likely deviation is R18 on the FCC indicator LEDs, which is labelled 100 m\u03a9 where its matching blue-LED resistors are 100 \u03a9, so LED6 would be effectively unlimited in current. A lower-confidence note is that the PWM driver's A0 pin is strapped high, giving 0x41 rather than the specified 0x40.\"\n}",
